Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 06:25:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/36] clk: ingenic: x1600: fix SADC gate bit

SADC and UART0 are assigned to the same CLKGR0 bit 14 even though
they are independent clocks. Disabling the unused SADC clock can
therefore gate the active UART0 clock and break the console.

Use bit 13 for SADC, matching the hardware clock layout and leaving
bit 14 exclusively assigned to UART0.
---
 drivers/clk/ingenic/x1600-cgu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/ingenic/x1600-cgu.c b/drivers/clk/ingenic/x1600-cgu.c
index ae4be18d4..5fd362c84 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/ingenic/x1600-cgu.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/ingenic/x1600-cgu.c
@@ -496,7 +496,7 @@ static const struct ingenic_cgu_clk_info x1600_cgu_clocks[] = {
 	[X1600_CLK_SADC] = {
 		"sadc", CGU_CLK_GATE,
 		.parents = { X1600_CLK_EXCLK, -1, -1, -1 },
-		.gate = { CGU_REG_CLKGR0, 14 },
+		.gate = { CGU_REG_CLKGR0, 13 },
 	},
 
 	[X1600_CLK_UART0] = {
-- 
2.55.0

